From 355d0acb85834b72542058f26ee5ea40a470eb33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:08:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix WebDAV backup listing and add a backup confirmation

Uploading backups to WebDAV servers like NutStore worked, but the
restore listing always came back empty. The multistatus parser
compared raw element names from XmlPullParser against plain local
names, while namespace processing is disabled - so the qualified
names the servers actually send ("d:response", "d:href", ...) never
matched and no file was ever picked up. Strip the namespace prefix
before comparing, in both the WebDAV and the S3 list parsers (the
S3 one defensively: ListObjectsV2 responses are usually unprefixed).

"Back up now" also asks for confirmation before uploading, showing
the retention count: after clearing local data, an accidental tap
would otherwise push an empty backup to the top of the restore
list.
---
